LancerFit backend
=================

REST API and realtime server for LancerFit, the gamified fitness platform for
the Toldo Lancer Centre at the University of Windsor. It serves both clients:
the student mobile app (lancer-fit_mobile) and the staff admin console
(lancer-admin).

Node.js, Express 5, TypeScript, Sequelize on PostgreSQL, Socket.IO, JWT.


Quick Start
-----------

	npm install
	cp .env.example .env        # then fill in DB and JWT values
	npm run dev                 # ts-node-dev on http://localhost:8000

	npm run build               # tsc -> dist/
	npm start                   # node dist/index.js

Docker:

	docker compose up

REST base is /api. Socket.IO listens on the same port and origin without the
/api suffix.


Essential Documentation
-----------------------

All maintainer documentation lives in docs/:

* docs/architecture.md   - layering, request path, where to add code
* docs/data-model.md     - every table, field, relation and invariant
* docs/api.md            - complete endpoint reference
* docs/realtime.md       - Socket.IO rooms and event contract
* docs/gamification.md   - XP, levels, streaks, quests, badge engine
* docs/operations.md     - environment, database, seeding, deployment
* docs/maintenance.md    - known gaps, traps, dead code, work queue

Read docs/architecture.md first. Read docs/maintenance.md before you trust
anything to be finished.


Layout
------

	src/index.ts        process entry: express, sequelize sync, seed, socket
	src/config/         database connection and startup seed
	src/routes/         URL to controller mapping only
	src/controllers/    request handling, transactions, responses
	src/services/       reusable domain logic (quests, badges, email)
	src/models/         Sequelize model definitions
	src/middleware/     auth, validation, error handling
	src/realtime/       Socket.IO server and emit helpers
	src/utils/          jwt, password, serializers, push, season
	src/validators/     zod request schemas


Conventions
-----------

* Every response body the frontends consume is produced by a function in
  src/utils/serializers.ts. Controllers never hand a raw model to res.json.
* Every controller is wrapped in asyncHandler so throws reach errorHandler.
* Any write that touches more than one table runs inside a transaction.
* Routes declare their own auth: authenticate for any signed-in user,
  authorize("admin") for staff-only.
* Static route paths are registered before parameterised ones.


Who Are You?
------------

* New maintainer: docs/architecture.md, then docs/data-model.md.
* Adding an endpoint: docs/api.md has the shape and the checklist.
* Debugging the mobile or admin client: docs/realtime.md and docs/api.md.
* Continuing the project: docs/maintenance.md is the handover.